Apple is requiring a &#36;9.99 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/icloud/">iCloud</a>+ plan to use the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> Home app features with a single <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit/">HomeKit</a> camera, and iPhone users aren't happy about it.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/iOS-26-Home-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1034994" /><br/>
&zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; includes text-based descriptions for motion alerts, a feature that uses &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj;. It recognizes people, animals, vehicles, packages, and general motion, and summarizes what's happening.<br/>
<br/>
During the beta, we learned that a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/06/ios-27-home-app-features-icloud/">2TB iCloud+ plan</a> or higher would be needed to use video summaries, but at the time, Apple didn't say how many cameras would be supported.<br/>
<br/>
Last week, Apple <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/127901">shared new details</a> on &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; limits, and it turns out the 2TB &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan priced at &#36;9.99 per month will only add AI summaries to a single camera. You'll need the &#36;29.99 per month 6TB plan to get AI summaries for two cameras, or the &#36;59.99 per month 12TB plan if you want to add up to five cameras. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-one/">Apple One</a> Premier subscribers are limited to a single camera since the bundle includes 2TB of &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ storage.<br/>
<br/>
Apple isn't offering an &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan that lets users receive AI summaries for an unlimited number of cameras.<br/>
<br/>
Using <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit-secure-video/">HomeKit Secure Video</a> cameras has always required a paid &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan, but the recording limits are at odds with the &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; limits. You can use a single &zwnj;HomeKit Secure Video&zwnj; camera with a &#36;0.99 per month 50GB &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan, five cameras with the &#36;2.99 per month 200GB plan, and unlimited cameras with the 2TB plan priced at &#36;9.99 per month.<br/>
<br/>
Someone who has a 2TB &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan and has invested in multiple &zwnj;HomeKit Secure Video&zwnj; cameras will only be able to use the new &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; feature with one of those cameras.<br/>
<br/>
There are <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/HomeKit/comments/1wdk9wk/the_future_of_apple_home_is_a_subscription/">dozens of complaints</a> about the subscription requirements <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/HomeKit/comments/1wgcfby/apple_one_only_supports_apple_intelligence_for/">on Reddit</a> and on the <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-changed-terms-for-homekit-camera-summaries-with-icloud.2489320/"><em>MacRumors</em> forums</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple warns that supported camera counts and other &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan features could change over time. There will also be usage limits on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI, photo editing tools, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/image-playground/">Image Playground</a>, with paid options to increase access. Apple hasn't announced pricing for features other than the &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; Home app options.<br/>
